     "\r\n<div lang=\"FR\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hi all,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I forward you two questions I just posted on stackoverflow.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">In <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/tRophicPosition/vignettes/Short_guide_to_tRophicPosition.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/tRophicPosition/vignettes/Short_guide_to_tRophicPosition.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497445620000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ALBqX8vByKDxaq4lXVuHb\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/tRophicPosition/vignettes/Short_guide_to_tRophicPosition.html</a>, it is written :<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">&quot;An essential component of the model to estimate trophic position is the trophic discrimination factor (TDF). By default the function loadIsotopeData() returns </span>Δ<span lang=\"EN-US\">N (3.4 ± 0.98 sd) and </span>Δ<span lang=\"EN-US\">C (0.39 ± 1.3 sd) based on Post’s (2002) assumptions. But you can change this assumption to use any values, simply adding them as arguments within the call to this function.&quot;<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The deltaN and deltaC arguments can indeed be fed with a list of values for these TDF. But instead of a list of values, is it possible to input mean and sd, as these are often given in the literature instead of a list of raw values ?<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">By the way, I have another question : when we run multiSpeciesTP with two Baselines, is alpha forced to be in [0;1] range (as for me it could be theoretcially be out odf this range, at least if it is the same alpha as the one in the formula from Post 2002 paper in Ecology) ?<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I thank you very luch<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Cheers,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Samuel<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><img width=\"100\" height=\"27\" style=\"width:1.0416in;min-height:.2833in\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/trophicposition-support/attach/384e5339e9f75/image001.png?part=0.1\" alt=\"logo-signature-inrae\"></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"color:#00a3a6\">Samuel WESTRELIN</span></b><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"color:blue\">samuel.w...@inrae.fr</span></a></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#00a3a6\"> </span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\">Ingénieur/chercheur</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\">Unité de recherche RECOVER</span></b><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\"> </span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\">Tél. : <a href=\"tel:+33%204%2042%2066%2069%2071\" value=\"+33442666971\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">+33 4 42 66 69 71</a></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\"> </span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;color:#00a3a6\">3275 Route de Cézanne</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;color:#00a3a6\">CS 40061</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\">13182 Aix en Provence Cedex 5 - France</span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#00a3a6\"> </span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><a href=\"https://www.inrae.fr/centres/provence-alpes-cote-dazur\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.inrae.fr/centres/provence-alpes-cote-dazur&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497445620000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0FWZoFc2JlPw_CU2NzPqTB\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:blue\">inrae.fr</span></b></a></span><span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span> </span><u></u><u></u></p></div></div>"
